https://github.com/chiragsakhuja/lc3tools/blob/d8409060241d35bb31fce0ced534e63e150b54f1/LICENSE

Upstream Licensing & Header Discrepancy:
-----------------------------------------
The original LC3tools repository was distributed publicly with a top-level 
Apache License 2.0. However, individual source code files retain localized, 
restrictive header text:

"Copyright 2020 McGraw-Hill Education. All rights reserved. No reproduction 
or distribution without the prior written consent of McGraw-Hill Education."

This clear legal contradiction regarding distribution permissions is noted and 
documented in the upstream repository's public issue tracker here:
https://github.com/chiragsakhuja/lc3tools/issues/10

In strict compliance with Section 4 of the Apache 2.0 License, all original 
copyright and attribution notices are preserved verbatim within the source 
files of this repository.

This downstream variant strips away the original project's GUI and documentation,
isolating the core C++ build mechanics into a modernized, rewritten CMake compilation
environment.
